# ${package}

Implement `${source}`. This package is automatically discovered by colcon in
the repository workspace; no registry or central package list needs editing.

From the AachenRover repository root:

```bash
./scripts/rover build
./scripts/rover launch ${package} ${node}.launch.py
# Override the namespace, configuration file, or simulation clock:
./scripts/rover launch ${package} ${node}.launch.py namespace:=my_sensor use_sim_time:=true
```

Configuration lives in `config/params.yaml`. Use `params_file:=/absolute/path.yaml`
for a deployment-specific configuration. Parameters are read at startup;
restart after changing them. Use simulation time only with a `/clock` publisher.

Edit `package.xml` for additional ROS dependencies. C++ dependencies also need
`find_package` and `ament_target_dependencies` in CMakeLists.txt. Install missing
dependencies with rosdep as documented in the repository, then rebuild. Python
third-party imports also need an appropriate rosdep or Python dependency.
Set real maintainer metadata before distributing the package. Add behavior tests
when implementing the worker; this scaffold does not test an unimplemented device.

This node is not automatically started with the simulation or physical robot.
Launch it explicitly, or include its launch file in a deployment bringup launch.
